+Extracting columns into lookup tables
+-------------------------------------
+
+Use ``--extract=column_name`` to extract all values for a column into a separate
+lookup table. The original values will be replaced by integer references to rows
+in that table, and a foreign key relationship will be created.
+
+For example, this extracts the ``breed`` column into a table named ``breed``::
+
+    $ sqlite-utils insert dogs.db dogs dogs.json --extract=breed
+
+The lookup table will contain one row for each distinct value, so repeated values
+in the input data will reference the same row. Use ``--extract`` more than once to
+extract multiple columns::
+
+    $ sqlite-utils insert dogs.db dogs dogs.json \
+        --extract=breed --extract=size
+
